      "font_size": 41,
      "text_bbox": [
        632,
        1266,
        1758,
        1536
      ],
      "text": "There are also large bronze statues of men arrayed\nagainst each other for battle: one is named\nErechtheus, the other Eumolpus. Yet those among the\nAthenians who have knowledge of ancient tradition\nhave not forgotten that it was in fact Immaradus, son\nof Eumolpus, who was slain by Erechtheus."
